# Line endings.
#
# This repository has no .gitattributes and developer checkouts on Windows run
# with core.autocrlf=true, so every text file — including shell scripts — was
# checked out with CRLF. docker/Dockerfile.db-init COPYs
# docker/db-init-entrypoint.sh out of the build context, so an image built on
# Windows carried a CRLF entrypoint and died immediately with
#
#     /app/docker/db-init-entrypoint.sh: set: line 20: illegal option -
#
# (`sh` reads `-eu\r` as a flag). The committed blob is LF, so CI on
# ubuntu-latest built and ran fine and nothing surfaced the breakage; it only
# appeared when the image was built from a Windows checkout. The same exposure
# applies to scripts/backup.sh and scripts/docker-start.sh.
#
# Normalise text in the repository and force LF on checkout for everything that
# is executed by a POSIX shell or copied into a Linux image.
* text=auto

*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile*     text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
.env.example    text eol=lf

# Binary: never translated, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.pdf binary
*.keystore binary
*.jar binary
